Title: THE LIGHTHOUSE
Credit: Pilot
Author: Your Name
Draft date: First draft

# ACT ONE

= Mara's routine is broken by an unexpected arrival.

EXT. SKERRY ROCK LIGHTHOUSE - DUSK

Waves hammer the rocks. A single window glows at the top of the tower.

INT. LAMP ROOM - CONTINUOUS

MARA (40s, weathered, unhurried) winds the brass clockwork. She checks her watch against it.

MARA
(to herself)
Right on time. As always.

A HORN sounds, low and far off. Mara freezes.

She crosses to the glass. Out on the water, a boat's lights — where no boat should be.

MARA
It's Thursday.

[[Establish earlier that the boat only ever comes on Mondays.]]

EXT. JETTY - NIGHT

The supply boat bumps against the pilings. OWEN (60s), the skipper, throws a line. Behind him, a YOUNG MAN in a city coat grips the rail, pale.

OWEN
Brought you company, Mara.

MARA
I didn't order any.

YOUNG MAN
Nobody ever does.

CUT TO:
